# Uldaros Theorix: a copy of a card that is cast is a cast spell (CR 707.12), and when the copy of a permanent spell resolves it
# becomes a token (CR 707.10f) - so "if you cast him" holds for that token and its enters ability triggers. Bot1 Entombs a
# second Uldaros on turn 1 and, on turn 5, casts the first with Black Lotus: his ability exiles the Uldaros in the graveyard
# (a creature) and the sacrificed Lotus (an artifact), and Bot1 casts a copy of the Uldaros for 6. The token Uldaros enters and
# its own ability triggers: it exiles Dark Ritual (the one card left that fits a type) and casts a copy of it. Uldaros is
# legendary (CR 704.5j), so one of the two is put into the graveyard (the default choice, the token, which ceases to exist); the proof that the token's ability
# triggered is Dark Ritual in exile, which only that ability could target.

